# Security Policy

## Supported Versions

Security updates are currently provided for the latest stable version of AFileTidy.

| Version | Supported |
|---|---|
| 1.0.x | Yes |
| Older versions | No |

## Reporting a Vulnerability

If you discover a security issue in AFileTidy, please avoid publishing sensitive details publicly before the issue can be reviewed.

Examples of security-related issues may include:

- Unexpected file deletion
- Files being moved to unintended locations
- Path traversal issues
- Unsafe handling of file or folder names
- Unexpected execution of external commands
- Problems that could lead to data loss
- Malicious behavior triggered by specially crafted files or folders

When reporting a security issue, please include:

- The AFileTidy version
- Your Windows version
- A clear description of the issue
- Steps to reproduce it
- Screenshots or error messages, if relevant

For non-sensitive bugs and feature requests, please use the GitHub Issues section.

## Important Notice

AFileTidy performs file-management operations on folders selected by the user.

Although the application is designed to organize files without deleting them, users should keep backups of important data before using any file-management software.

Only download AFileTidy from the official repository:

https://github.com/ozkancantasarim/AFileTidy
